          "title": "You'll want to know: ढलान",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ढलान — ḍhalān — \"a slope\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ढलान पर गाड़ी धीरे चलाइए। ḍhalān par gāṛī dhīre calāiye. Drive slowly on the slope."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ढलान (ḍhalān) is built on the stem of ढलना, \"to slope, to go down\", which goes back to ḍhalati, \"bends over, falls\", a form CDIAL reconstructs (CDIAL 5581); CDIAL does not list the noun itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
